=== Freezing overlay ===
{{Infobox screen effect
|title=Freezing overlay 
|image=Frozen effect.png
|camera=Yes
|hud={{Jebe|Yes|No}}
|graphics=All{{needs testing|java=1}}
|options=None
}}
The freezing overlay is a circular formation of crystals and snow flakes that appears when the player is freezing in [[powder snow]]. This effect slowly fades in until it is at full opacity.

If the player equips leather armor while freezing, this overlay fades out slowly, then disappears.
{{-}}
=== Pumpkin blur ===
{{Infobox screen effect
|title=Carved pumpkin blur
|image=Pumpkin blur.png
|camera=No
|hud={{Jebe|No|Yes}}
|graphics=All
|options=None
|image2=Pumpkin blur BE.png}}
The pumpkin blur is a cut-out shape of the carved pumpkin's face that appears when wearing a [[carved pumpkin]]. {{IN|je}}, the texture is stretched to the edges of the screen; {{In|be}}, the texture is placed in the middle of the screen, with dark edges filling the rest.
{{-}}
=== Spyglass scope ===
{{Infobox screen effect
|title=Spyglass scope
|image=Spyglass scope.png
|camera=No
|hud={{Jebe|No|Yes}}
|graphics=All
|options=None
}}
The spyglass scope is a brown square in the middle of the screen that appears when using a [[spyglass]]. This scope effect quickly zooms in when using a spyglass, until the top and bottom are partly covered.
{{-}}

== Animated sprites and models ==

=== Mining Fatigue ===
{{Infobox screen effect
|title=Elder Guardian ghost
|image=Elder guardian curse.gif
|camera=Yes
|hud=Yes
|graphics=No
|options=None
|image2=ElderGuardianCurseBedrock.gif}}
{{conjecture|section=1}}
When within a spherical radius of 50 blocks of an [[elder guardian]], the player is inflicted with [[Mining Fatigue]] III. This is indicated by a ghost of an elder guardian appearing in the player's view, which moves from the top of the screen to the bottom.

{{IN|Java}}, this occurrence is considered a particle effect; it can be summoned with the {{cmd|particle minecraft:elder_guardian}} command.

{{IN|Bedrock}}, this occurrence is caused by a separate mob called the [[Elder Guardian Ghost|elder guardian ghost]]. However, when it is summoned using {{cmd|summon
minecraft:elder_guardian_ghost}}, it is invisible and rises to the sky.

The model of the elder guardian is used for this effect. This means that changing the texture and model associated with the elder guardian also changes what appears on the player's screen.
{{-}}

=== Totem of Undying ===
{{Infobox screen effect|title=Totem of Undying|image=Totem of Undying Animation.gif|camera=Yes|hud={{jebe|No|Yes}}|image2=Totem of Undying Bedrock Animation.gif}}The effect appears when a [[Totem of Undying|totem of undying]] is used. The totem spins to the middle of the screen and disappears. 
{{IN|Java}}, the totem of undying effect is a full 3D model. 
{{IN|Bedrock}}, the totem of undying effect is a 2D texture.
{{-}}

=== Hero of the Village ===
{{Infobox screen effect|title=Hero of the Village|image=Hero of the Village Bedrock Animation.gif|camera=Yes|hud=Yes}}
{{exclusive|bedrock|section=1}}
This effect appears when the player obtains [[Hero of the Village]] from defeating a [[raid]]. This effect does not happen when the effect is given through commands. It is similar to the totem of undying effect.
{{-}}
=== Raid Omen ===
{{Infobox screen effect|title=Raid Omen|image=Raid Omen Bedrock Animation.gif|camera=Yes|hud=Yes}}
{{exclusive|Bedrock|section=1}}
This screen effect appears when the player enters a village while under the [[Bad Omen]] effect, converting it into [[Raid Omen]]. This effect does not appear when giving Raid Omen through commands, and it looks similar to the totem of undying effect.
{{-}}

==Transformations==

===Damage tilt===
[[File:Damage tilt.png|thumb|Damage tilt effect]]
{{IN|Java}}, when the player receives damage, the screen tilts to the direction opposite of the entity or block who damaged the player. 

{{IN|Bedrock}}, when the player receives damage, the screen tilts to the right regardless of the damage direction.

The strength of damage tilting can be adjusted in the settings.

===View bobbing===
View bobbing is a toggleable feature that adds a slight movement of the screen from left to right when walking. It also affects items and blocks in the player's hand.

===Distortion effects===
These effects are seen when the player either goes through a nether portal or has the nausea status effect. Different levels do not affect the distortion. However, the effect can be affected by changing the distortion effect setting.{{Only|Java}}

===FOV based changes===
While sprinting, flying, swimming or while affected by a speed effect, the FOV (field of view) increases. The FOV decreases when being affected by the slowness effect, while using a spyglass, by using a bow, or by going into water or powder snow. The FOV can be changed in settings with a minimum of 30, and a maximum of 110. Different levels of slowness or speed affect the FOV more than others.

FOV effects can be toggled in the settings.

=== Camera shake ===
{{Exclusive|bedrock|section=1}}
With the {{Cmd|camerashake}} command, a player's camera can perform a shaking effect. This can be either positional (shaking the camera position) or rotational (shaking the camera direction). The effect can be disabled in the settings.<gallery>
File:Minecraft_Bedrock_Positional_Camerashake.gif|Example of a positional camera shake
File:Minecraft_Bedrock_Rotational_Camerashake.gif|Example of a rotational camera shake
</gallery>

